    ],
    "versions": {
      "leb": [
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 13,
          "text": "Then Balak said, “Please walk with me to another place where you will see them, but you will only see part of them and will not see all of them; and curse them for me from there.”",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 14,
          "text": "So he took him to the field of Zophim to the top of Pisgah, and he built seven altars, and he offered a bull and a ram on each altar.",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 15,
          "text": "Balaam said to Balak, “Station yourself here at the burnt offering while I myself meet with Yahweh there.”",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 16,
          "text": "Then Yahweh met with Balaam, and he put a word in his mouth, and he said, “Return to Balak, and you must speak thus.”",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 17,
          "text": "He came to him, and behold, he was standing at his burnt offering, and the princes of Moab with him. And Balak said to him, “What has Yahweh spoken?”",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 18,
          "text": "Then he uttered his oracle, and said,\n“Stand up, Balak, and hear;\nlisten to me, son of Zippor!",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 19,
          "text": "God is not a man, that he should lie,\nnor a son of humankind,\nthat he should change his mind.\nHas he said, and will he not do it?\nAnd has he spoken, and will he not fulfill it?",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 20,
          "text": "&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Behold, I have received a command to bless;\nwhen he has blessed, I cannot cause it to return.",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 21,
          "text": "&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;He has no regard for evil in Jacob,\nand he does not see trouble in Israel;\nYahweh his God is with him,\nand a shout of a king is among them.",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 22,
          "text": "&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;God, who brings them out from Egypt,\nis like the strength of a wild ox for them.",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 23,
          "text": "&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Because there is no sorcery against Jacob,\nand there is no divination against Israel.\nNow it will be said to Jacob and Israel,\nwhat God has done!",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 24,
          "text": "Look! the people will rise like the lion;\nhe raises himself and will not lie down\nuntil he eats the prey\nand drinks the blood of the slain.”",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 25,
          "text": "Then Balak said to Balaam, “Do not curse them at all, nor bless them at all!”",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 26,
          "text": "But Balaam answered and said to Balak, “Did I not speak to you, saying, ‘Whatever Yahweh speaks I will do’?”",
          "isHeading": false
        }
      ],
      "nirv": [
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 13,
          "text": "Balaam’s Second Message From God\nThen Balak said to Balaam, “Come with me to another place. You can see the people of Israel from there. You will see only some of them. You won’t see all of them. From there, put a curse on them for me.”",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 14,
          "text": "So Balak took Balaam to the field of Zophim. It was on the highest slopes of Pisgah. There he built seven altars. He offered a bull and a ram on each altar.",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 15,
          "text": "Balaam said to Balak, “Stay here beside your offering. I’ll meet with the Lord over there.”",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 16,
          "text": "The Lord met with Balaam. He put a message in Balaam’s mouth. The Lord said, “Go back to Balak. Give him my message.”",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 17,
          "text": "So he went to him. He found him standing beside his offering. The princes of Moab were with him. Balak asked him, “What did the Lord say?”",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 18,
          "text": "Then Balaam spoke the message he had received from God. He said,\n“Balak, rise up and listen.\nSon of Zippor, hear me.",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 19,
          "text": "God isn’t a mere man. He can’t lie.\nHe isn’t a human being. He doesn’t change his mind.\nHe speaks, and then he acts.\nHe makes a promise, and then he keeps it.",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 20,
          "text": "He has commanded me to bless Israel.\nHe has given them his blessing. And I can’t change it.",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 21,
          "text": "“I don’t see any trouble coming on the people of Jacob.\nI don’t see any suffering in Israel.\nThe Lord their God is with them.\nThe shout of the King is among them.",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 22,
          "text": "God brought them out of Egypt.\nThey are as strong as a wild ox.",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 23,
          "text": "There isn’t any magic that can hurt the people of Jacob.\nNo one can use magic words to harm Israel.\nHere is what will be said about the people of Jacob.\nHere is what will be said about Israel.\nPeople will say, ‘See what God has done!’",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 24,
          "text": "The people of Israel are going to wake up like a female lion.\nThey are going to get up like a male lion.\nThey are like a lion that won’t rest\nuntil it eats what it has caught.\nThey are like a lion that won’t rest\nuntil it drinks the blood of what it has killed.”",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 25,
          "text": "Then Balak said to Balaam, “Don’t put a curse on them at all! And don’t give them a blessing at all!”",
          "isHeading": false
        },
        {
          "book": "Num",
          "chapter": 23,
          "verse": 26,
          "text": "Balaam answered, “Didn’t I tell you that I have to do only what the Lord says?”",
          "isHeading": false
        }
      ],
